  "published": "2026-10-28T18:35:43.56Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "dotskit keeps a solution up with the template, keeping the team's changes.\n\n- A solution keeps up with the template: dotskit adds services and flags to it and upgrades it to a new version, keeping the team's changes.\n- A service generated into a solution adds itself to All.sln.\n- Email by flag, with a sandbox that keeps a test stand from mailing real people.\n- MongoDB by flag, beside the main database.\n- Containers run on a read-only filesystem.\n- The test servers start with one command, the same on a developer's machine as in CI.\n- Coverage on demand, with a report per service.\n- The solution is generated with --Solution; -M false still works.\n- The template answers to the short name dotskit too: dotnet new dotskit.\n\nHow to update a solution generated from an earlier version: https://github.com/sawking-tech/DotNetSolutionKit/blob/v2.8.0/docs/getting-started/upgrading.md",
